= Appendix B: Matrix Theory

This appendix presents the essential results of matrix theory needed throughout the course. Matrices arise naturally in the study of linear transformations, group representations, and certain cryptographic constructions such as the Hill cipher. An understanding of basic matrix operations, determinants, and systems of linear equations is assumed.

